event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":686,"item_id":"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb43345034819181be552d4fa9af75","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_candidate\\\":1,\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/propositions/-\\\",\\\"value\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M015\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For any measurable space (X,Σ), measure μ, and real normed additive commutative group V, the integral over X of the identically zero V-valued function is zero.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"X\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"type with measurable space Σ\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"μ\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"measure on X\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"V\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"real normed additive commutative group\\\"}],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"X\\\",\\\"μ\\\",\\\"V\\\"],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"MeasureTheory.integral_zero\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Bochner.Basic\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"V is a normed additive commutative group and real normed space.\\\",\\\"X has a measurable space and μ is a measure on X.\\\"],\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For any measurable space (X,Σ), measure μ, and real normed additive commutative group V, the integral over X of the identically zero V-valued function is zero.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M015-0016/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"680de6f0e3792b01d2303a5f4c8b17c7ba484f3636c65e3f065d36ecf57903bd\\\"}]}}},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/inputs\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"N001\\\",\\\"N002\\\",\\\"N003\\\",\\\"N004\\\",\\\"M015\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"N003 gives E′(r)=2∫_{ℝⁿ} h(x) dx, where h(x)=u_t(x,r)·(u_{tt}(x,r)−Δ_xu(x,r)). N004 says h(x)=0 for every x, so this integrand is the identically zero real-valued function. Apply M015 with X=ℝⁿ, μ=Lebesgue measure and V=ℝ: its whole-space integral is zero. Hence E′(r)=0. Together with N001 and N002 this proves all three clauses for arbitrary r>0.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/uses\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"N003\\\",\\\"N004\\\",\\\"M015\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/applications/-\\\",\\\"value\\\":{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M015\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"X=ℝⁿ with its Borel measurable space; μ=Lebesgue measure; V=ℝ; the integrand is h(x)=u_t(x,r)·(u_{tt}(x,r)−Δ_xu(x,r))=0 for every x by N004.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"ℝ is a normed additive commutative group and real normed space.\\\",\\\"ℝⁿ has its declared measurable space and Lebesgue measure.\\\",\\\"N004 identifies the integrand pointwise with the zero function.\\\"]}}]}\"}"}

